lback); every resize uses the selected scrollback and must fit the same budget. Supply a smaller terminal shape when that product is too large; dimensions are never clamped. A command name resolves through the inherited PATH; the working directory defaults to the caller's current directory; host environment variables are inherited with scenario overrides. Environment keys cannot contain '=' or NUL, and REA_PROCESS_RUN_ID is reserved for process ownership. Filesystem snapshots are opt-in through filesystem_observation_paths. A positive finalization_ms makes a timeout or idle deadline send SIGTERM to the captured root through its start identity, keep observing, and send SIGKILL once after the interval; exit.finalization records each attempt with its delivery result and the observed exit, and cancellation still ends the run at once. The target runs with the current user's permissions; this is not a security sandbox.", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "properties": {"executable": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema0", "description": "Command name or executable path to run."}, "arguments": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema2"}, "working_directory": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema3"}, "environment": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema4"}, "filesystem_observation_paths": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema5"}, "terminal": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema6", "description": "The visible terminal and scrollback together must use at most 1,000,000 xterm renderer cells: columns \u00d7 (rows + scrollback). Resize events use the same scrollback and limit."}, "events": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema10"}, "timeout_ms": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema12"}, "idle_timeout_ms": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema14"}, "settle_ms": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema15"}, "finalization_ms": {"$ref": "#/$defs/__schema16", "description": "Milliseconds a target may keep running after SIGTERM when timeout_ms or idle_timeout_ms fires, before SIGKILL; 0 sends SIGKILL immediately. Both signals reach the ca